course: dictionary
lesson: 12906
title: A formal word: erroneous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Erroneous is a formal word. It means wrong, or containing a mistake. «The answer was erroneous, so the marks were taken away.» The clue is in the sentence: the answer was not correct, so it was erroneous.
explain: Test the meaning by swapping in an easy word. In «an erroneous answer», does wrong fit? Yes, so erroneous means wrong here too. Use this check whenever you meet a long, serious-sounding word.
explain: Scientists use erroneous when a measurement goes wrong. «The scale gave an erroneous reading, so the test had to be done again.» Reports and news use it in the same stiff, careful way.
explain: In everyday talk we say wrong or mistaken instead. Both mean nearly the same thing, but erroneous sounds more formal and exact. Knowing it helps you read reports and exam questions.
fact: Erroneous means wrong or containing a mistake.
fact: Erroneous is a formal word, used in reports, news and exams.
fact: «An erroneous answer» is an answer that is wrong.
fact: «An erroneous belief» is a belief that is not true.
fact: In everyday speech, people say wrong or mistaken instead of erroneous.
exercise: «She gave an erroneous answer to the sum, so the teacher marked it wrong.» What does erroneous mean? | Written in pencil | Correct and clever | *Wrong | Long and difficult
exercise: Which everyday word means nearly the same as erroneous? | Quiet | Beautiful | *Mistaken | Fast
exercise: The science report said, «The erroneous result came from a broken thermometer.» What does erroneous mean here? | A result that was very large | A result found in a book | *A measurement that went wrong | A perfect and careful measurement
test: «The map had an erroneous road on it, so we got lost.» What does erroneous mean? | *Wrong | Hidden | Painted blue | Brand new
test: «Ravi held an erroneous belief that bats are birds.» What is an erroneous belief? | *A belief that is not true | A happy belief | A belief about the weather | A belief shared by everyone
exam: A news report says, «The erroneous figures were corrected today.» What does this mean? | The figures were read aloud | *The figures were wrong and have now been fixed | The figures were perfect and were printed twice | The figures were lost forever
